<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n829" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγρ-εύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hunter</i>, epith. of Aristaeus, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				9.65
			</span></i>; of Apollo, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				200
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Herod.
				3.34
			</span></i>; of Bacchus, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				1192
			</span></i> (lyr.); of Poseidon, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Pisc.</u>
				47
			</span></i>; of Pan, <i><span class="en">
				Apollod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of an arrow, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.75
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			a kind of bird, <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				8.24
			</span></i>. (From <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγρός</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκεύς</span> : <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶκος</span>; the reference to hunting is secondary.)</div>
